==English==

===Etymology===
US, 19th century. {{m|en|peeled|Peeled}} probably refers to keeping one's eyelids retracted.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-keep one's eyes peeled.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|[[keep]]<,,kept> [[one's]] [[eye]]s [[peeled]]}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive|idiomatic|(with "for")}} To be [[on the alert]], to be [[watchful]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1990|title={{w|Jurassic Park}}|author={{w|Michael Crichton}}|text=And directly below is our Mesozoic jungle river -- where, if you are lucky, you just may catch a glimpse of a very rare carnivore. '''Keep your eyes peeled''', everyone!}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2003-11-14|title=Sailing into the past|author=Laura Bly|work=USA Today|text=lookouts posted to the port and starboard bows '''keep their eyes peeled''' for the ghostly outline of approaching traffic.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|to be watchful}} {{l|en|keep an eye out}}, {{l|en|keep one's eyes open}}

